     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear hBayesDM developers,<div><br></div><div>Thanks for this brilliant toolbox. I would like to add new models but I had issues compiling new models.</div><div><br></div><div>Therefore, I did a simple test: I created two stan files and corresponding Yaml files with models that are identical to existing ones but with different model names.</div><div><br></div><div>I then generated R and python3 codes using the script <span style=\"color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13.600000381469727px;background-color:rgba(27,31,35,0.0470588)\">hBayesDM/commons/generate-codes.sh </span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(36,41,46);font-size:13.600000381469727px;background-color:rgba(27,31,35,0.0470588)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(36,41,46);font-size:13.600000381469727px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">All seemed good so far.</font></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13.600000381469727px;background-color:rgba(27,31,35,0.0470588)\"><br></span></div><div>Finally I tried to install the R package but I get the error message posted below, where bandit4arm_combLR_lapse* are the names of the files that I have added (identical to the bandit4arm_lapse* files but with a different name).</div><div><br></div><div>Any idea of what the problem might be? I have the latest python and hBayseDM version, running on a Mac Os Mojave 10.14.</div><div><br></div><div>I would be very grateful for some help!</div><div><br></div><div>Best wishes,</div><div><br></div><div>Flavia</div><div><br></div><div><p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:14px;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Andale Mono&quot;;color:rgb(47,255,18);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.901961)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\">Rscript -e &#39;devtools::install()&#39;</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:14px;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Andale Mono&quot;;color:rgb(47,255,18);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.901961);min-height:16px\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\"></span><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:14px;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Andale Mono&quot;;color:rgb(161,161,161);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.901961)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures;color:#2fb41d\">✔</span><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures;color:#2fff12\">  </span><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\">checking for file ‘/Users/flavia/GitHub/hBayesDM-1.0.2/R/DESCRIPTION’</span><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures;color:#2fff12\"> ...</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:14px;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Andale Mono&quot;;color:rgb(161,161,161);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.901961)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\">─  preparing ‘hBayesDM’:</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:14px;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Andale Mono&quot;;color:rgb(161,161,161);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.901961)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures;color:#2fb41d\">✔</span><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures;color:#2fff12\">  </span><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\">checking DESCRIPTION meta-information</span><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures;color:#2fff12\"> ...</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:14px;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Andale Mono&quot;;color:rgb(161,161,161);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.901961)\"><span style=\"font-variant-ligatures:no-common-ligatures\">─  cleaning src</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:14px;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Andale Mono