     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Flavia,<div><br></div><div>It seems that DESCRIPTION file does not have information for new R files. In order to solve the issue, you should generate documentation before building or installing the package. Could you try running the following commands?</div><div><br></div><div>```</div><div>devtools::build()  # In order to build first to make a C++ header file</div><div>devtools::document()  # Update DESCRIPTION from R files</div><div>devtools::install()</div><div>```</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Jaeyeong</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Tuesday, December 3, 2019 at 8:36:01 PM UTC+9, Flavia Mancini wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear hBayesDM developers,<div><br></div><div>Thanks for this brilliant toolbox. I would like to add new models but I had issues compiling new models.</div><div><br></div><div>Therefore, I did a simple test: I created two stan files and corresponding Yaml files with models that are identical to existing ones but with different model names.</div><div><br></div><div>I then generated R and python3 codes using the script <span style=\"color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13.600000381469727px;background-color:rgba(27,31,35,0.0470588)\">hBayesDM/commons/generate-codes.sh </span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(36,41,46);font-size:13.600000381469727px;background-color:rgba(27,31,35,0.0470588)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(36,41,46);font-size:13.600000381469727px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">All seemed good so far.</font></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13.600000381469727px;background-color:rgba(27,31,35,0.0470588)\"><br></span></div><div>Finally I tried to install the R package but I get the error message posted below, where bandit4arm_combLR_lapse* are the names of the files that I have added (identical to the bandit4arm_lapse* files but with a different name).</div><div><br></div><div>Any idea of what the problem might be? I have the latest python and hBayseDM version, running on a Mac Os Mojave 10.14.</div><div><br></div><div>I would be very grateful for some help!</div><div><br></div><div>Best wishes,</div><div><br></div><div>Flavia</div><div><br></div><div><p st