    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\">Hi Flavia,<div><br></div><div>It seems that DESCRIPTION file does not have information for new R files. In order to solve the issue, you should generate documentation before building or installing the package. Could you try running the following commands?</div><div><br></div><div>```</div><div>devtools::build()  # In order to build first to make a C++ header file</div><div>devtools::document()  # Update DESCRIPTION from R files</div><div>devtools::install()</div><div>```</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Jaeyeong</div><div><br>On Tuesday, December 3, 2019 at 8:36:01 PM UTC+9, Flavia Mancini wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear hBayesDM developers,<div><br></div><div>Thanks for this brilliant toolbox. I would like to add new models but I had issues compiling new models.</div><div><br></div><div>Therefore, I did a simple test: I created two stan files and corresponding Yaml files with models that are identical to existing ones but with different model names.</div><div><br></div><div>I then generated R and python3 codes using the script <span style=\"color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13.600000381469727px;background-color:rgba(27,31,35,0.0470588)\">hBayesDM/commons/generate-codes.sh </span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(36,41,46);font-size:13.600000381469727px;background-color:rgba(27,31,35,0.0470588)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(36,41,46);font-size:13.600000381469727px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">All seemed good so far.</font></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13.600000381469727px;background-color:rgba(27,31,35,0.0470588)\"><br></span></div><div>Finally I tried to install the R package but I get the error message posted below, where bandit4arm_combLR_lapse* are the names of the files that I have added (identical to the bandit4arm_lapse* files but with a different name).</div><div><br></div><div>Any idea of what the problem might be? I have the latest python and hBayseDM version, running on a Mac Os Mojave 10.14.</div><div><br></div><div>I would be very grateful for some help!</div><div><br></div><div>Best wishes,</div><div><br></div><div>Flavia</div><div><br></div><div><p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:14px;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Andale Mono&quot;;color:rgb(47,255,18);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.901961)\"><span>Rscript -e &#39;devtools::install()&#39;</span></p><p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:14px;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Andale Mono&quot;;color:rgb(47,255,18);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.901961);min-height:16px\"><span></span><br></p><p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:14px;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Andale Mono&quot;;color:rgb(161,161,161);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.901961)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(47,180,29)\">✔</span><span style=\"color:rgb(47,255,18)\"> <span> </span></span><span>checking for file ‘/Users/flavia/GitHub/hBayesDM-1.0.2/R/DESCRIPTION’</span><span style=\"color:rgb(47,255,18)\"><span> </span>...</span></p><p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:14px;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Andale Mono&quot;;color:rgb(161,161,161);background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.901961)\"><span>─  preparing ‘hBayesDM’:</span></p><p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-s